<title>UK: John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 12.1% in week.</title>
<headline>John Lewis weekly UK store sales up 12.1% in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The John Lewis Partnership said its UK department store sales rose 12.1 percent in the week to November 16 compared with the same week a year earlier.</p>
<p>In the 16 weeks to November 16, sales were up 14.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Total sales, including those of the Waitrose supermarket chain, rose 10.4 percent in the week and were up 12 percent in the 16-week period.</p>
<p>-- Mike Peacock London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
